[Term]
id: GO:0090009
name: primitive streak formation
def: "The developmental process pertaining to the initial formation of the primitive streak from unspecified parts. The primitive streak is a ridge of cells running along the midline of the embryo where the mesoderm ingresses. It defines the anterior-posterior axis." [GOC:dph, GOC:sdb_2009, GOC:tb]
