property_value: RO:0002175 NCBITaxon:9606
property_value: UBPROP:0000001 "Dermal bone that forms the antero-lateral region of the palate and is located ventral to the autopalatine. The dermopalatine is bilaterally paired and usually bears teeth.[TAO]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-08-14", external_class="TAO:0000015", ontology="TAO", source="TAO:GA_TG"}
property_value: UBPROP:0000005 "Dermopalatine: same as palatine. The prefix is used by fish people because the palatine is a dermal replacement bone for a section of the autopalatine section of the palatoquadrate. In that context, palatine is potentially ambiguous.[Palaeos]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-09-17", source="http://palaeos.com/vertebrates/glossary/glossaryD.html"}
property_value: UBPROP:0000005 "In ostariophysans, the dermopalatine is absent.[TAO]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-09-06", external_class="TAO:0000015", ontology="TAO", source="Curator"}
property_value: UBPROP:0000008 "Fusion of dermopalatine+autopalatine." xsd:string

[Term]
id: UBERON:0001685
name: hyoid bone
def: "A horseshoe shaped bone situated in the anterior midline of the neck between the chin and the thyroid cartilage. The hyoid bone provides attachment to the muscles of the floor of the mouth and the tongue above, the larynx below, and the epiglottis and pharynx behind. [WP,modified]." [Wikipedia:Hyoid_bone]
