[Term]
id: UBERON:0001810
name: nerve plexus
def: "Anatomical junction where subdivisions of two or more neural trees interconnect with one another to form a network through which nerve fibers of the constituent nerve trees become regrouped; together with other nerve plexuses, nerves and ganglia, it constitutes the peripheral nervous system. Examples: cervical nerve plexus, brachial nerve plexus, sacral nerve plexus[FMA]." [FMA:5901, https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1306, Wikipedia:Nervous_system_plexus]
subset: human_reference_atlas
subset: human_subset
subset: mouse_subset
subset: uberon_slim
