property_value: RO:0002175 NCBITaxon:9606
property_value: UBPROP:0000001 "The fourth metacarpal bone (metacarpal bone of the ring finger) is shorter and smaller than the third. The base is small and quadrilateral; its superior surface presents two facets, a large one medially for articulation with the hamate, and a small one laterally for the capitate. On the radial side are two oval facets, for articulation with the third metacarpal; and on the ulnar side a single concave facet, for the fifth metacarpal[Wikipedia:Fourth_metacarpal_bone]." xsd:string {source="Wikipedia:Fourth_metacarpal_bone"}
property_value: UBPROP:0000104 "4" xsd:nonNegativeInteger

