[Term]
id: UBERON:0004341
name: primitive streak
def: "The primitive streak is a structure that forms during the early stages of avian, reptilian and mammalian embryonic development[WP]. the midline ridge of the embryonic epiblast that later develops into mesoderm and endoderm[MP]." [MP:0002231, Wikipedia:Primitive_streak]
