relationship: capable_of GO:0055078 ! sodium ion homeostasis
relationship: confers_advantage_in ENVO:00000447
relationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:7742 ! Vertebrata <vertebrates>
property_value: RO:0002161 NCBITaxon:40674
property_value: UBPROP:0000008 "In sharks, salt glands are found in the rectum, but in birds and reptiles, they are found in or on the skull, in the area of the eyes, nostrils or mouth. In crocodiles, the salt is excreted through the tongue. Such glands work by active transport via sodium-potassium pump that moves salt from the blood into the gland, where it can be excreted as a concentrated solution. Salt glands function to keep salt balance, and allow marine vertebrates to drink seawater" xsd:string

