property_value: foaf:depiction "http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b5/Hodenschema.svg" xsd:anyURI
property_value: UBPROP:0000001 "Any of a group ranging from one to twelve (varies in species) small seminal ducts per testis which transport sperm from the testes to the kidney.[AAO]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-06-20", external_class="AAO:0010532", ontology="AAO", source="AAO:BJB"}
property_value: UBPROP:0000008 "There are two basic designs for efferent ductule structure: a) multiple entries into the epididymis, as seen in most large mammals. In humans and other large mammals, there are approximately 15-20 efferent ducts, which also occupy nearly one third of the head of the epididymis. b) single entry, as seen in most small animals such as rodents, whereby the 3-6 ductules merge into a single small ductule prior to entering the epididymis" xsd:string
property_value: UBPROP:0000012 "Check EMAPA" xsd:string {external_ontology="EMAPA"}

