property_value: UBPROP:0000001 ". [][VHOG]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-09-17", external_class="VHOG:0000970", ontology="VHOG", source="http://bgee.unil.ch/"}
property_value: UBPROP:0000003 "In all jawed vertebrates the first arch forms the jaw, while the second arch forms the hyoid apparatus. These two arches are separated by the first pharyngeal pouch and cleft.[well established][VHOG]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-09-17", external_class="VHOG:0000970", ontology="VHOG", source="DOI:10.1016/j.semcdb.2010.01.022 Grevellec A, Tucker AS, The pharyngeal pouches and clefts: development, evolution, structure and derivatives. Seminars in Cell and Developmental Biology (2010)", source="http://bgee.unil.ch/"}
