[Term]
id: UBERON:0010853
name: capitulum of humerus
def: "A smooth, rounded eminence on the lateral portion of the articular surface of the humerus. It articulates with the cupshaped depression on the head of the radius, and is limited to the front and lower part of the bone." [Wikipedia:Capitulum_of_the_humerus]
subset: human_reference_atlas
subset: human_subset
subset: mouse_subset
synonym: "capitellum" RELATED [Wikipedia:Capitulum_of_the_humerus]
synonym: "capitulum humeri" RELATED OMO:0003011 [Wikipedia:Capitulum_of_the_humerus]
synonym: "capitulum of humerus" RELATED [Wikipedia:Capitulum_of_the_humerus]
synonym: "dorsal condyle of the humerus" RELATED SENSU [Wikipedia:Capitulum_of_the_humerus]
synonym: "humeral capitulum" EXACT [FMA:23373]
xref: FMA:23373
xref: SCTID:282816008
xref: Wikipedia:Capitulum_of_the_humerus
is_a: UBERON:0005055 ! zone of long bone
relationship: part_of UBERON:0009988 {source="FMA"} ! condyle of humerus
property_value: editor_note "TODO - check AAO." xsd:string {source="WP"}
property_value: foaf:depiction "http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b9/Capitulumhumeri.PNG" xsd:anyURI
property_value: RO:0002175 NCBITaxon:9606
property_value: UBPROP:0000008 "In birds, where forelimb anatomy has adaptation for flight, its functional if not ontogenetic equivalent is the dorsal condyle of the humerus" xsd:string
property_value: UBPROP:0000008 "The Capitulum humeri is present in Carnivora, more distinctly in the cat than in the dog. The Fossa coronoidea, present in the cat is medial to the Fossa radialis and accommodates the Processus coronoideus medialis ulnae when the elbow is flexed. A Foramen supratrochleare occurs in carnivora and occasionally in pig.[NOMINA ANATOMICA VETERINARIA (2005)]" xsd:string

