[Term]
id: UBERON:0013447
name: sagittal crest of skull
def: "A ridge of bone running lengthwise along the midline of the top of the skull of many mammalian and reptilian skulls and serves as an attachment site for the temporailis muscle[WP,modified]." [Wikipedia:Sagittal_crest]
subset: human_subset
subset: mouse_subset
synonym: "crista sagittalis externa" EXACT []
synonym: "sagittal crest" BROAD []
synonym: "sagittal ridge" RELATED []
xref: Wikipedia:Sagittal_crest
is_a: UBERON:0005913 ! zone of bone organ
relationship: part_of UBERON:0003113 ! dermatocranium
property_value: foaf:depiction "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/43/Paranthropus_aethiopicus.JPG" xsd:anyURI
property_value: UBPROP:0000008 "Skulls of some dinosaur species, including tyrannosaurs, possessed well developed sagittal crests. Among mammals, dogs, cats, lions, and many other carnivores have sagittal crests, as do some leaf eaters, including tapirs and some apes. Sagittal crests are found in robust great apes, and some early hominins. Prominent sagittal crests are found among male gorillas and orangutans, and do occur but only rarely in male chimpanzees such as Bili Apes" xsd:string
property_value: UBPROP:0000009 "The sagittal crest serves primarily for attachment of the temporalis muscle, which is one of the main chewing muscles" xsd:string
property_value: UBPROP:0000012 "Compare with: AAO:0000384 parasagittal crest (UBERON:0013402)" xsd:string {external_ontology="AAO"}

